@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+# Knowledge Base
+
+An Electron desktop app for reading your documents and asking questions about them. Every answer cites the passages it came from.
+
+## Run
+
+```bash
+npm install
+npm run dev      # builds main/preload/renderer and launches Electron
+npm test         # service tests (vitest)
+npm run check    # typecheck
+```
+
+On first launch, click **Load sample documents**, or import your own `.txt` / `.md` files with **+ Import** or by dragging them onto the sidebar.
+
+## How it works
+
+- **Import**: files are validated (type, ≤ 5 MB, not binary, not empty), copied into the app data directory, and indexed straight away.
+- **Indexing**: text is split into ~500-character passages at paragraph boundaries. Long paragraphs are split by sentence, and headings stay with the section they introduce.
+- **Answering**: BM25 retrieval ranks passages, then the best-matching sentences (and lists, kept whole) are pulled out as the answer, each with a `[n]` citation. Click a citation to open the document with that passage highlighted. Questions the documents don't cover get "couldn't find anything" rather than a guess.
+- **Optional LLM answers**: start the app with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set (and optionally `KB_MODEL`, default `claude-opus-5-5`), and Claude writes the answer from the top retrieved passages, citing them. Those passages are sent to the Anthropic API. Without the key, everything stays local. If the API call fails, the app falls back to the local answer.
+
+Data lives in `<userData>/knowledge-base-data` (the path is logged on startup).
+
+## Layout
+
+- `src/main`: window, IPC handlers (ids are validated, file dialog runs in main)
+- `src/preload`: sandboxed `contextBridge` API (`window.knowledgeBase`)
+- `src/services`: persistence (atomic writes, path-contained), documents, indexing, retrieval, Q&A
+- `src/renderer`: React UI (document list, viewer, Q&A panel)
+- `tests/`: service tests against the sample documents
